message.content:
The product is an aluminum clamp with a post that adapts a stationary exercise bicycle to accept a standard bicycle stem and handlebars. It is a part or accessory of stationary exercise equipment, so heading 9506 fits best. Subheading 9506.91 covers articles and equipment for general physical exercise, gymnastics or athletics, and its parts and accessories fall under 9506.91.00. The specific 10-digit statistical suffix I would use is 9506.91.0030 (parts and accessories of exercise equipment).

The alternative is heading 8714 (bicycle parts), but it excludes parts of stationary exercise cycles, which belong in 9506. This follows the usual CBP treatment of stationary exercise bike parts, and I did not look up a specific ruling.

{"hts_code": "9506.91.0030", "reason": "An aluminum adapter that mounts to a stationary exercise bicycle frame to accept bicycle stems and handlebars is a part or accessory of exercise equipment, classified in 9506.91 rather than bicycle parts in 8714."}
